  "description": "Bowire.Mcp — exposes the Bowire workbench itself as an MCP server, so AI agents (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Copilot) can drive discovery, invocation, recording, mocking, and replay through the Model Context Protocol. Sibling of Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Mock; the third row of the MCP surface area: Bowire as MCP server for its own operations (Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Protocol.Mcp covers the other two — Bowire as MCP client and as MCP adapter for fremd-protocols). Built on the official ModelContextProtocol C# SDK (2.0.x, MCP revision 2026-07-28). Mount via `services.AddBowireMcp() + endpoints.MapBowireMcp(...)` for the Streamable-HTTP transport, or run `bowire mcp serve` for stdio.",
